            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.736,
            0.047,
            0.846,
            0.064
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Number Play"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.085,
            0.478,
            0.109
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What is the 100th even number?"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.118,
            0.382,
            0.136
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This is 2 × 100 = 200."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.137,
            0.846,
            0.174
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Does this help in finding the 100th odd number? Let us compare the sequence of evens and odds term-by-term."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.174,
            0.536,
            0.192
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Even Numbers:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " 2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12,..."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.175,
            0.192,
            0.536,
            0.209
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Odd Numbers:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " 1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 11,..."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.21,
            0.847,
            0.266
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We see that at any position, the value at the odd number sequence is one less than that in the even number sequence. Thus, the 100th odd number is 200 – 1 = 199."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.274,
            0.583,
            0.297
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Write a formula to find the "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "n ^ { \\mathrm { t h } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " odd number."
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.306,
            0.848,
            0.345
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us first describe the method that we have learnt to find the odd number at a given position:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.206,
            0.349,
            0.846,
            0.387
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(a) Find the even number at that position. This is 2 times the position number."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.207,
            0.391,
            0.644,
            0.41
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(b) Then subtract 1 from the even number."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.41,
            0.525,
            0.429
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Writing this in expressions, we get"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.208,
            0.434,
            0.285,
            0.452
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(a) 2n"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.208,
            0.458,
            0.316,
            0.475
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(b) "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "2 n - 1"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.476,
            0.847,
            0.515
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus, 2n is the formula that gives the "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "n ^ { \\mathrm { t h } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " even number, and 2n – 1 is the formula that gives the "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "n ^ { \\mathrm { t h } }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " odd number."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.534,
            0.587,
            0.558
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "6.3 Some Explorations in Grids"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.449,
            0.971,
            0.55,
            0.985
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.567,
            0.662,
            0.643
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Observe this 3 × 3 grid. It is filled following a simple rule — use numbers from 1 – 9 without repeating any of them. There are circled numbers outside the grid."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
